<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Exposition&nbsp;time</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Time&nbsp;over</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;Führer&quot; is a German title which basically means &quot;leader&quot; or &quot;guide&quot;, was a term used usually for the head of a political party or other large organization. It's still used as the &quot;guide&quot;, usually along the lines of oberführer, which alternately gets translated as &quot;overwatcher/overseer&quot;, but NEVER gets used in a political context for obvious reasons.</p>
<p>The show was also explicitly set in the 19-teens, judging by dates seen on gravestones and such.</p>
<p>And he was named King because he was hand picked amongst a group of kids who were raised to become the next leader of Amestris, and just the first one to survive the stone-implantation to become a Homunculus. That wasn't exactly the type of upbringing associated with humility!</p>
</div>
